.TH BPOPSIM 1 "2026-11-07" "bpopsim 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bpopsim \- simulate asexual population evolution under serial transfer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bpopsim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-output\-\fIKIND\fR
.RI [ \-\-output\-KIND ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bpopsim
simulates a population of asexual cells propagated by serial transfer. In
each transfer the population grows by binary division for a fixed number of
generations, is diluted by binomial sampling back to its starting size, and
the cycle repeats. Beneficial mutations arise at a per-division rate with
fitness effects drawn from a chosen model. Every genotype that ever arose is
kept in an ancestry tree, from which the program reports genotype and clade
frequencies over time, line-of-descent statistics, and a Muller matrix.
.PP
At least one
.B \-\-output\-*
option must be given.
.SH GENERAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print step-by-step details of the run to standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Perform extra internal consistency checks (population size bookkeeping).
.SH SIMULATION OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-rng\-seed " \fIN\fR"
Seed for the random number generator. 0 (the default) chooses a random seed
and prints it, so any run can be reproduced later.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-replicates " \fIN\fR"
Number of independent replicate populations (default 1). All replicates draw
from one random stream, so a seed reproduces the whole set.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-initial\-population\-size " \fIN\fR"
Number of cells at the start of the simulation (default 5E6).
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-population\-size\-after\-transfer " \fIN\fR"
Number of cells after each dilution (default 5E6).
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-generations\-per\-transfer " \fIG\fR"
Doublings per transfer (default 6.64, a 1:100 dilution). The dilution factor
is 2^G.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-number\-of\-transfers " \fIN\fR"
Number of transfers to simulate after burn-in (default 50).
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-initial\-fitness " \fIW\fR"
Fitness of the ancestral genotype (default 1.0).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-mutation\-rates " \fIRATES\fR"
Beneficial mutation rate per cell division for each category of mutations
(default 1E-7). Categories are written as comma-separated items inside
|-separated groups, where a group collects categories drawn from the same
kind of distribution, for example
.BR "\-u \[dq]1E-7,1E-8|1E-9\[dq]" .
Repeating the option adds another group. A mutation occurs at the total rate
over all categories and is assigned to one category in proportion to its
rate. Quote the value so the shell does not treat | as a pipe.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-fitness\-effects " \fIEFFECTS\fR"
Fitness effect of a mutation in each category (default 0.1), with the same
| and , shape as
.BR \-u .
Under the exponential model this is the mean.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fitness\-effect\-model " \fIMODELS\fR"
How the fitness effect is drawn in each category, with the same shape as
.BR \-u ,
or a single letter applied to every category (default u):
.B u
every mutation has exactly the
.B \-s
value;
.B e
effects are exponentially distributed with that mean;
.B o
exactly the
.B \-s
value, but only one mutation in that category can ever occur in a lineage.
Example matching the
.B \-u
example above:
.BR "\-f \[dq]u,u|e\[dq]" .
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-multiplicative\-fitness
Combine effects multiplicatively, fitness = f (1 + s), instead of additively,
fitness = f + s.
.TP
.BR \-1 ", " \-\-first\-mutation\-fitness\-effects " \fIS\fR"
Fix the fitness effects of the first, second, ... mutations in any lineage.
Give the option once per mutation. These override
.B \-s
until a lineage has more mutations than values given.
.TP
.BI \-\-average\-fitness\-end\-condition " W"
Stop a replicate once mean fitness reaches W (default 0, off).
.SH MARKER DIVERGENCE OPTIONS
Marker mode models a population founded by N genotypes that differ only in a
neutral marker (for example Ara+ and Ara- in the long-term evolution
experiment). Every descendant inherits its founder's marker, so the marker
fractions track which founding lineage is winning.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-marker\-states " \fIN\fR"
Start with the population split equally into N genotypes, each carrying a
different marker state and 1/N of the cells (default 0, off; otherwise at
least 2). N larger than the population size leaves markers with less than
one cell, which die at the first transfer.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-marker\-divergence\-end\-fraction " \fIF\fR"
End a replicate once the most common marker state makes up at least F of
the population (default 0, off). Requires
.BR \-k .
.TP
.B \-\-output\-marker\-frequencies
Write
.IR marker_frequencies.tab :
one row per replicate and marker state, with the fraction of the population
carrying that marker at each recorded transfer. Requires
.BR \-k .
.PP
In marker mode the ancestry tree has N root genotypes. The line-of-descent
outputs
.RB ( \-\-output\-diverged\-frequencies ", " \-\-output\-longest\-sweep\-time )
follow only the first root and are not meaningful.
.SH OUTPUT OPTIONS
All output files are tab-separated text written to the output folder.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output\-folder " \fIDIR\fR"
Directory for output files, created if needed (default the current
directory).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-burn\-in " \fIN\fR"
Perform N transfers before recording begins. These are in addition to
.BR \-n .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-coarse\-graining " \fIN\fR"
Record statistics only every N transfers (default 1).
.TP
.B \-\-output\-average\-fitness
Write
.IR average_fitness.tab :
mean fitness per recorded transfer, one row per replicate.
.TP
.B \-\-output\-average\-mutations
Write
.I average_mutations.tab
and
.IR average_mutations_category_N.tab :
mean number of mutations per cell, in total and per category.
.TP
.B \-\-output\-genotype\-frequencies
Write
.IR genotype_frequencies_MIN_REP.dat :
frequency over time of every genotype that was ever at or above
.BR \-\-minimum\-output\-frequency .
.TP
.B \-\-output\-clade\-frequencies
Write
.IR clade_frequencies_MIN_REP.dat :
the same for clades (a genotype together with all its descendants). Header
rows mark which clades lie on the line of descent to the final dominant
genotype and give each founding mutation's fitness effect.
.TP
.BI \-\-minimum\-output\-frequency " F"
Threshold for the two options above (default 0.01).
.TP
.B \-\-output\-diverged\-frequencies
Write
.IR mutation_divergence_depth_frequency_D.tab
for D from 1 to
.BR \-\-diverged\-mutation\-depth :
the largest clade frequency at each transfer among clades diverged from the
final dominant line of descent by at least D mutations.
.TP
.BI \-\-diverged\-mutation\-depth " N"
Maximum D for the option above (default 10).
.TP
.B \-\-output\-longest\-sweep\-time
Write
.IR longest_sweep_time.tab :
per replicate, the longest time in transfers for a mutation on the final line
of descent to rise from at most 5% to at least 95% frequency.
.TP
.B \-\-output\-muller
Write
.IR muller_matrix_REP.dat :
a Muller matrix with
.B \-\-muller\-resolution
rows per recorded transfer. Cell values are genotype ids; see
.I src/R
and
.I src/python
for plotting scripts.
.TP
.BI \-\-muller\-resolution " N"
Vertical resolution of the Muller matrix (default 200).
.TP
.B \-\-muller\-lod
Give genotypes on the line of descent to the final dominant negative ids so
they can be colored separately.
.SH EXAMPLES
Three replicates with daily 1:100 transfers for 500 days, recording mean
fitness and Muller matrices:
.PP
.nf
.RS
bpopsim -r 3 -p 5E6 -N 5E6 -T 6.64 -u 1E-7 -s 0.1 -n 500 \\
    -o output --output-average-fitness --output-muller
.RE
.fi
.PP
Two categories of beneficial mutation, exponentially distributed effects:
.PP
.nf
.RS
bpopsim -u 1E-7 -s 0.05 -u 1E-9 -s 0.3 -f e -n 200 \\
    -o output --output-clade-frequencies
.RE
.fi
.SH REPRODUCIBILITY
Given the same seed, GSL version, and command line, output is identical on
every platform. The seed used is always printed at the start of a run.
.SH SEE ALSO
The GNU Scientific Library manual, chapter "Random Number Generation".
